          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 8. HOW WE USE -->
      <section id="how-we-use" aria-labelledby="h-use">
        <h2 id="h-use" class="section-heading">How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <div class="card">
          <p class="body-text mb-3">
            We process personal data strictly for the purposes described below. We do not use personal data
            for automated decision-making or profiling that produces legal or similarly significant effects.
          </p>
          <ul class="bullet-list">
            <li>
              <strong>Application operation</strong> — authenticating registered users, storing and
              synchronising your plant library, photos and discoveries across your devices, and delivering
              AI results.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Local notifications</strong> — scheduling on-device care reminders based solely on
              the schedules you configure. This processing occurs entirely on your device.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>AI processing</strong> — transmitting photographs, language preference, local weather
              data and, for diagnoses, the plant&apos;s prior history to Google Gemini on your behalf, and
              returning the result to you.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Care advice from local conditions</strong> — where you consented to location, looking up
              current weather for your coordinates via Open-Meteo.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>User support</strong> — using the email address, display name and message sent with
              in-app feedback solely to investigate and answer your enquiry.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Security and integrity</strong> — rate-limiting requests by IP address, device and
              account to detect and prevent abuse of our APIs and of the AI capacity we pay for.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Legal compliance</strong> — processing data where required to fulfil a legal or
              regulatory obligation applicable to us.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="footnote mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
            <strong>We do not</strong> use personal data to serve targeted or behavioural advertising,
            build user profiles for marketing, or share data with data-brokerage services.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 9. STORAGE, SECURITY & RETENTION -->
      <section id="storage-security" aria-labelledby="h-storage">
        <h2 id="h-storage" class="section-heading">Storage, Security and Retention</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">

          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="card-title">Where Your Data Lives</h3>
            <div class="body-text space-y-2">
              <p>
                Our application server and its Postgres database are hosted on <strong>Railway</strong>.
                Photographs that we store are held in <strong>Cloudflare R2</strong> object storage. Both are
                third-party infrastructure providers acting as our processors, and both are named in
                <a href="#sharing" class="link">Section&nbsp;11</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                All communication between the Application and our servers uses TLS-encrypted connections
                (HTTPS). Encryption at rest for the database and for object storage is provided by those
                infrastructure providers.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="card-title">On-Device Storage</h3>
            <p class="body-text">
              User preferences are held in encrypted local storage on your device. Session authentication
              tokens are stored exclusively within the operating system&apos;s secure credential store (iOS
              Keychain or Android Keystore) and are accessible only by the Application process.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="card-title">Security Measures — and Their Limits</h3>
            <ul class="bullet-list mb-3">
              <li>Passwords are stored only as BCrypt hashes; plaintext passwords are never stored or accessible to us.</li>
              <li>Access to systems that hold personal data is restricted to authorised personnel on a need-to-know basis.</li>
              <li>Identification and diagnosis images are held in memory for the duration of the request and are never written to our storage or backups.</li>
              <li>Uploaded images are re-encoded, which strips EXIF metadata including embedded GPS coordinates.</li>
              <li>
                <strong>Stored plant and discovery photos are not access-controlled.</strong> They sit in a
                public-read bucket at predictable addresses, as described in
                <a href="#photos" class="link">Section&nbsp;4</a>. We disclose this rather than describe those
                photos as private.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>There is no email verification and no password reset by email.</strong> We do not send
                email to users at all, so account recovery and identity confirmation by email are not
                available and should not be relied on.
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="body-text">
              No method of electronic transmission or storage is entirely secure. While we implement
              commercially reasonable safeguards, we cannot guarantee absolute security. To report a potential
              security vulnerability, please contact us at
              <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="link">{contactEmail}</a>.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="card-title">Retention</h3>
            <div class="overflow-x-auto -mx-1">
              <table class="w-full text-[14px] min-w-[480px] border-separate border-spacing-0">
                <thead>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50">
                    <th scope="col" class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 border-b border-gray-200 rounded-tl-lg">Data</th>
                    <th scope="col" class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 border-b border-gray-200 rounded-tr-lg">Retained for</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100">
                  {retention.map(([what, howLong]) => (
                    <tr class="bg-white hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors">
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">{what}</td>
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-500">{howLong}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="card !border-emerald-200 !bg-emerald-50/50">
            <h3 class="card-title !text-emerald-800">Account Deletion Is Immediate</h3>
            <p class="body-text mb-3">
              When you delete your account, deletion happens <strong>straight away — not on a queue and not
              on a 30-day timer</strong>. We remove:
            </p>
            <ul class="bullet-list">
              <li>your user record;</li>
              <li>all plants, care schedules and care logs;</li>
              <li>all scan and diagnosis history;</li>
              <li>all discoveries, including their stored coordinates;</li>
              <li>all authentication tokens; and</li>
              <li>all associated photographs in our image storage.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="footnote mt-3">
              Rate-limiting records tied to your requests are not deleted individually; they expire on their
              own within 24 hours. Uninstalling the Application removes locally stored data from that device
              but does not by itself delete your account.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 10. INTERNATIONAL TRANSFERS -->
      <section id="international-transfers" aria-labelledby="h-transfers">
        <h2 id="h-transfers" class="section-heading">International Data Transfers</h2>
        <div class="card body-text space-y-3">
          <p>
            Photographs and related context sent for AI processing are handled by <strong>Google
            Gemini</strong> (Google LLC), which may process data on servers located in the United States or
            other jurisdictions outside the European Economic Area (&ldquo;EEA&rdquo;) or the United Kingdom.
            Where you consented to location processing, your coordinates are sent to
            <strong>Open-Meteo</strong>; in-app feedback containing your email address and name is transmitted
            through <strong>Resend</strong>; and our hosting and image storage providers,
            <strong>Railway</strong> and <strong>Cloudflare</strong>, may also process data outside the EEA
            and the UK.
          </p>
          <p>
            Where such transfers occur, we rely on the transfer mechanisms offered by each provider, including
            Standard Contractual Clauses where applicable. In respect of transfers to the United States,
            Google LLC participates in and is certified under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework and the UK
            Extension thereto. You may review Google&apos;s data-processing terms and transfer mechanisms at
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Separately, note that photographs stored in our public-read bucket are reachable from anywhere in
            the world by anyone holding the address, as described in
            <a href="#photos" class="link">Section&nbsp;4</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

