        <div class="card body-text space-y-3">
          <p>
            If you are a California resident, the California Consumer Privacy Act as amended by the CPRA
            gives you the rights below. The categories of personal information we collect, the purposes for
            which we use them, and the parties to whom we disclose them are set out in
            <a href="#information-we-collect" class="link">Sections&nbsp;3 to 6</a> and
            <a href="#sharing" class="link">Section&nbsp;11</a>. In CCPA terms, the categories we collect are
            identifiers (email address, display name, provider user ID, IP address), internet or network
            activity limited to rate-limiting records, geolocation data where you consented, and visual
            information (your photographs).
          </p>
          <ul class="bullet-list">
            <li><strong>Right to know</strong> the categories and specific pieces of personal information we have collected, their sources, the purposes, and the categories of third parties to whom we disclosed them.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to delete</strong> personal information we hold about you.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to correct</strong> inaccurate personal information.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to limit</strong> the use of sensitive personal information. We use precise geolocation only for the weather lookup and discovery records described in <a href="#location" class="link">Section&nbsp;5</a>, and for no other purpose.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to non-discrimination</strong> for exercising any of these rights.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            <strong>We do not sell or share personal information</strong> as those terms are defined by the
            CCPA/CPRA, and we have not done so in the preceding twelve months. We do not use or disclose
            personal information for cross-context behavioural advertising. To exercise a California right,
            email <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="link">{contactEmail}</a>; you may use an
            authorised agent, and we will verify your request against the account details we hold.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 14. CHILDREN -->
      <section id="children" aria-labelledby="h-children">
