              In the <strong>European Economic Area and the United Kingdom</strong>, we do not knowingly
              collect personal information from children below the applicable age of digital consent in
              their country of residence, which is <strong>16 years</strong> in most EU member states
              unless a lower age (minimum 13) has been set by national law.
            </li>
            <li>
              In all other jurisdictions, we apply the higher of the locally applicable minimum age for
